From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:23:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Express the fee burn in basis points and validate it at start

Transaction.setBurnedFee(height) now burns
floor(fee x burn.feeBasisPoints / 10000); the typeof guard and the
parseInt are gone. validateMergedMilestones() requires, at every merged
milestone, a burn object whose feeBasisPoints is a safe integer from 0
to 10000, and refuses a feePercent key with a message that names
feeBasisPoints. Solar silently disabled the burn when feePercent was
the string "90"; that configuration now refuses to start. The mainnet
and testnet presets change feePercent 90 to feeBasisPoints 9000, which
burns exactly what Solar burned. burn.txAmount is not changed.

Test: patches/tests/23-burn-basis-points.test.js (fails on the
unpatched build, passes here).

Patch: 23
Consensus: yes
